    "reviewText": "I'll run this review pass: first load the buildwright framework and personas, then the requirement brief, then the working-tree diff.Now let me read the framework docs, personas, and the requirement brief in parallel.Framework loaded. Now the requirement brief and the full diff.Confirmed — this change is the uncommitted working tree only (the socket_base commit is merged PR #1255, out of scope). Now reading the brief and the actual changes.The implementation takes a \"delegate geo-routing to the content site\" approach — I need the design doc to see whether that was the sanctioned path, plus the tasks, new tests, and findings docs.The design explicitly sanctions the content-site delegation as the primary path with a runtime verification gate. Now the PR description, new tests, consumers, and the helper internals.All Help references route through the single helper/config key. One last confirmation — `brand_domains` in the config (the TLD-substitution test depends on it):# /bw-review — issue #1252 \"DTrader Help always opens EU help-centre URL\"\n\n**Target resolved:** the uncommitted working tree vs `master` — 4 modified files (`brand.config.json`, `packages/shared/src/utils/brand/brand.ts`, `packages/core/.../Footer/help-centre.jsx`, `sidebar.spec.tsx`) plus new tests, openspec artifacts, and findings docs. The one committed change on this branch (`f9e29fe752`, chart-freeze fix, PR #1255) is a separately merged PR and was excluded.\n\n---\n\n## Lens 1 — Requirement coverage\n\nRequirements derived independently from `proposal.md` (excluded as explicit non-goals in the change's own docs: fixing the trade.deriv.com redirect itself, language param on the URL, logged-in DIEL account override, any UI change):\n\n| # | Requirement (from the proposal) | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | Help destination is market-aware: EU visitors reach the EU help centre, everyone else the global one; no market-discarding hop | **COVERED** |\n| R2 | Unknown/missing/errored market signal defaults to the global (non-EU) help centre; opening never blocks or errors | **COVERED** |\n| R3 | All Help entry points (`dt_sidebar_help`, mobile Menu → Help centre, footer `dt_help_centre` incl. unmounted) resolve through one shared rule | **COVERED** |\n| R4 | Link mechanics preserved: new tab, `noopener,noreferrer`, labels/icons/test-ids unchanged | **COVERED** |\n| R5 | Behaviour-only fix, no visual change | **COVERED** |\n\n**R1** is implemented via the design's sanctioned primary path (design.md D1): the market-discarding `trade.deriv.com` hop is removed and the link goes straight to the deriv.com content site, which owns the regional IA and geo-routes its own visitors — so the destination is market-aware by delegation rather than by an in-app EU-country list. The non-EU half of the verification gate (task 1.2) was runtime-verified (Malaysian egress, 2026-08-26 → global page, no `/eu/`). The EU half could not be executed (no EU egress available in the implementation environment) and is recorded as a **before-production concession** in `docs/spec-to-pr/findings/before-production.md` — exactly the mechanism `framework/findings.md` and this command prescribe for such items. The failure mode if the EU lift were absent is bounded to the spec's own mandated safe default (EU visitor sees the global centre), never the reported misrouting, and the group-4 contingency (in-app resolver + `help_centre_url_eu`) is pre-broken-down in tasks.md. I classify this covered, with the logged concession flagged as an advisory release condition — not a code gap.\n\n**R2** holds structurally: the app-side URL is the global one, and both call sites keep the synchronous `window.open(getHelpCentreUrl(), '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer')` inside the click handler — nothing async was introduced that could block or pop an error.\n\n**R3** verified by repo sweep: the only help-centre URL sources left are the one config key and `getHelpCentreUrl()` (`brand.ts:202-204`); `sidebar.tsx:95` and `menu.tsx:50` already funnel through it (untouched), and the footer's divergent `StaticUrl href='/help-centre/'` was replaced with `href={getHelpCentreUrl()}`. No other entry point exists.\n\n**R4** verified: live call sites untouched (menu.spec passes unchanged, sidebar.spec keeps the same `window.open` assertion shape); the footer keeps `id='dt_help_centre'` and its aria-label on the same anchor element, and now carries `target='_blank'` + `rel='noopener noreferrer'` as the spec scenario requires — pinned by the new unit test.\n\n---\n\n## Lens 2a — SECURITY REVIEW (security-engineer persona)\n\n### Verdict: ✅ SECURE\n\n**Scans (scoped to the diff):** no `package.json`/lockfile changes → dependency audit not applicable to this change (repo-level residuals are pre-existing, tracked elsewhere); grep of the diff for secret-like strings → none; no SAST-relevant sinks introduced (the change is a config constant, a JSDoc, and anchor attributes).\n\n**Manual (OWASP pass over changed code):**\n- **A03/XSS:** no untrusted input reaches any sink. `getHelpCentreUrl()` returns a build-time config constant through `substituteDerivDomain()`, whose hostname substitution is gated on the `brand_domains` allowlist (`brand.ts:92-104`). No user-controlled data flows into the href.\n- **Reverse tabnabbing:** the new `target='_blank'` anchor correctly pairs with `rel='noopener noreferrer'`; both `window.open` call sites keep `'noopener,noreferrer'`. \n- **Comparative:** the change follows the existing brand-URL controls rather than weakening them; the divergent third URL-construction path in the footer was eliminated.\n\n**Passed checks:** no hardcoded secrets; no new network calls; no auth-surface change; open-redirect protections in `brand.ts` untouched.\n\n---\n\n## Lens 2b — CODE REVIEW (staff-engineer persona)\n\n### Verdict: ✅ APPROVED\n\n### Critical issues\nNone.\n\n### Recommendations\nNone reaching the ≥80 confidence bar.\n\n### Observations (advisory, non-blocking)\n- The configured URL `https://deriv.com/helpcentre/deriv-trader` 301s to the canonical hyphenated `https://deriv.com/help-centre/deriv-trader`. Pointing the config at the canonical form would drop one redirect hop; the PR description documents keeping the exact URL issue #1252 names as deliberate. Cosmetic.\n- `deriv.be`/`deriv.me` substituted destinations (`deriv.be/helpcentre/…`) are external IA this repo can't verify — the same class of unverified substitution as before the change (design D4 preserves it deliberately).\n- The before-production EU-egress check must actually be executed before release — already logged in the right place; releasing without it only risks the spec's safe default, not the reported bug.\n\n### What's good\n- Proof-of-red convention fully met: both new suites cite their red against the unfixed code with test names and expected/received values (pr-description.md \"Tests\"); the attribute assertions and the sidebar mock swap are honestly declared characterization.\n- Minimal-diff discipline: config + JSDoc + one component realignment; both live call sites untouched, contract proven by the unchanged menu spec. DRY/KISS/YAGNI honored — no speculative geo-resolver was built, but its contingency is pre-planned.\n- The upstream root cause is escalated as a `report-upstream` finding rather than silently patched around.\n\n---\n\nBoth lenses pass: all in-scope requirements are covered, no security or correctness defects were introduced, and the one open runtime item (EU-egress verification of the content site's lift) is a properly logged before-production concession with a bounded, spec-safe failure mode — a human should ensure it's executed before the production release.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVED"
